From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: shell32: a folder the user may not write to asks for an administrator

David: "If you try to copy to a protected place on the C: it should ask for
admin"; a paste into such a folder did nothing and said nothing. Now a copy,
move, delete or rename that would write where the user may not asks, as
Windows does: "Destination Folder Access Denied -- You'll need to provide
administrator permission to copy to this folder" with Continue (the shield)
and Cancel. Continue runs the same operation elevated (rundll32
shell32.dll,SgFileOperationElevated through the "runas" verb: the consent
prompt) and tells the folders shown to read themselves again.

Also: a copy that failed made SHFileOperation return 0 (the progress-aware
copy left no error behind); and files put on the clipboard without a
"Preferred DropEffect" were not pasted at all -- Windows copies them.

Gate: make test-fileopadmin (the question and Cancel; a failed copy's
error; a paste without a drop effect). The elevated copy: QA VM.
